  "disposition": "behavior_unchanged",
  "summary": "Bypass prepared-program reuse when Python builder dependencies cannot be resolved statically.",
  "regressions": [
    "Dynamic imports, aliased import_module and evaluated Python disable whole-program reuse.",
    "Two preparations with untracked builders rebuild the program while preserving safe full-IR kernel caching."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Full parity matrix remains deferred until an explicit user request; no baseline reconciliation.",
    "No shader arithmetic, native reference arithmetic, comparison tolerances or dispatch dependencies change.",
    "Compiler-cache schema changes once; subsequent documentation/test changes do not evict unchanged code. The conservative parity provenance envelope is unchanged.",
    "Compiler concurrency defaults to at most four isolated processes; NEXUS_TILELANG_COMPILE_JOBS=1..16 controls resource usage.",
    "Only code and schedules are cached. Fresh upload, validation, buffers and provenance are retained on every scene preparation."
  ]
